From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: restrict default CMA pool below 4 GiB

Without alloc-ranges, the 128 MiB default linux,cma pool is placed at
0x878000000 (~34 GiB), outside the 32-bit coherent DMA mask of ath11k. During
s2idle resume, dma-direct cannot allocate from that CMA pool and falls back to
the ZONE_DMA buddy allocator for order-7 and order-9 contiguous blocks while
compaction is disabled, resulting in page allocation failures.

Add alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x80000000 0x0 0x80000000> to linux,cma so the default
CMA pool is placed below 4 GiB and services 32-bit coherent DMA allocations.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -215,6 +215,14 @@
 		linux,cma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			size = <0x0 0x8000000>;
+			/*
+			 * Keep the default CMA pool below 4 GiB: without this it is
+			 * allocated top-down at 0x878000000, where devices with a
+			 * 32-bit coherent mask (ath11k/MHI) cannot use it and fall
+			 * back to high-order ZONE_DMA buddy allocations on every
+			 * resume.
+			 */
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x80000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
 			reusable;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
-- 
